      "text": "The root cause is that OpenQASM 2.0 `if` conditions must compare a whole classical register, so `if (c[0]==1)` is rejected. Changing those six conditions to `if (c==1)` fixes it. Since `c` is a single-bit register, that compares the same bit.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, execute\nfrom qiskit import BasicAer as Aer\n\n# FIX: if (c[0]==1) indexed a classical bit, which OpenQASM 2.0 conditionals do not allow -> changed each condition to compare the whole register, if (c==1), because c is a 1-bit register so this tests the same bit\ncloner1 = \"\"\"\nOPENQASM 2.0;\ninclude \"qelib1.inc\";\nqreg q[5];\ncreg c[1];\nx q[2];\nx q[4];\nx q[0]; //Set up input\nmeasure q[0] -> c[0];\nif (c==1) CX q[1],q[2];\nif (c==1) CX q[2],q[1];\nif (c==1) CX q[1],q[2];\nif (c==1) CX q[3],q[4];\nif (c==1) CX q[4],q[3];\nif (c==1) CX q[3],q[4];\nmeasure q[1]->c[0];\nmeasure q[3]->c[0];\n\"\"\"\n\ncircuit = QuantumCircuit.from_qasm_str(cloner1)\n\nbackend = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\njob = execute(circuit, backend, shots=1024)\nresult = job.result()\nprint(result.get_counts())\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
